---
import Store from '../layouts/Store.astro';
import ProductArt from '../components/ProductArt.astro';
import products from '../data/products.json';
import spec from '../../kb/specs/sample-specifications-v3.json';
---
<Store title="Sea & Stone · sample sheets v3"><div class="wrap"><section class="collection"><p class="eyebrow">COLLECTION 01 · SAMPLE DEVELOPMENT v3</p><h1>One design.<br/><em>Every detail.</em></h1><p class="lead">A shared identity.<br/>And a cup that tells its story in pictures.</p><p>The tee, bag and bottle proofs share the vector emblem and outlined lettering. The cup has its own continuous illustrated wrap. Material renders are concept impressions; the supplier must proof the current art on the actual blank.</p><p class="design-note">Proposed specifications are ready to discuss. They are not confirmed stock, purchase commitments or manufacturing approvals.</p><div class="actions" style="display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:24px"><a class="button" href="/artwork/sea-and-stone-v3/utkal-product-sheets-v3.pdf">Read the four product sheets ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/artwork/utkal-sample-pack-v3.zip" download>Download the sample review pack ↓</a></div></section>
{products.map((product,i)=>{const row=spec.products[i];return <section class="artwork-review"><div><div class="placement-proof"><img src={product.proof} alt={product.name+' current placement proof with shared emblem and outlined lettering'}/></div><p class="design-note">{product.id==='coffee-cup'?'Illustrative two-view render':'Current schematic placement'} · {row.language} · not to scale</p><details><summary>View the material concept</summary><ProductArt product={product}/><p class="design-note">AI-generated concept image, not a supplier sample. The current flat print file controls lettering and emblem geometry.</p></details></div><div><p class="eyebrow">{row.code} · {product.name}</p><h2>{product.id==='coffee-cup'?'A story in pictures.':'Sea & Stone.'}</h2><p>{product.description}</p><div class:list={['artwork-proof',{'dark':product.kind==='tee'||product.kind==='bottle'}]}><img src={product.artwork} alt={product.name+' current flat artwork v3'}/></div><p class="design-note">Proposed canvas: {row.size.join(' × ')} mm. {row.placement}</p><a href={product.artwork} download>{product.id==='coffee-cup'?'Download illustrated wrap ↓':'Download vector artwork ↓'}</a>{product.id==='water-bottle' && <p class="design-note">Two colour options: matte black and Nila Sagara blue. Both use the same artwork; the premium construction awaits supplier samples.</p>}<h3 style="margin-top:24px">Proposed specification</h3><p>{row.proposal}</p><p class="design-note">{row.base}</p></div></section>})}
<section class="closing" id="cup-colours"><p class="eyebrow">CUP COLOUR EXPLORATION</p><h2>Earth or sea.</h2><p>Two alternatives: Mankada Pathara terracotta with a riverbank scene, and Nila Sagara blue with a bolder sailing scene. Both keep UTKAL prominent.</p><img src="/images/cup-colour-exploration-v1.png" alt="Two alternative Utkal cup concepts: terracotta with ivory riverbank storytelling and sea blue with a laterite sailing boat" style="display:block;width:100%;height:auto"/><p class="design-note">AI-generated comparison concepts. Neither is selected; the current ivory cup and sample artwork remain the working version.</p></section><section class="closing"><p class="eyebrow">THE STORY CUP</p><h2>{spec.cup_story.title}</h2><p class="lead">{spec.cup_story.scenes.join(' · ')}</p><p class="design-note">The boat ritual and maritime remembrance are supported by the <a href={spec.cup_story.source_url}>Ministry of Culture</a>. The illustration connects remembrance, voyage and exchange; it does not claim to reconstruct one historical journey.</p><p>Next: confirm the proposed blanks and placements, obtain vendor templates and costs, then review physical samples. Only the T-shirt’s black base is already fixed.</p></section></div></Store>
